[C,docs/api.rst,372] Loaders
[C,docs/api.rst,373] -------
[C,docs/api.rst,374] 
[C,docs/api.rst,375] Loaders are responsible for loading templates from a resource such as the
[C,docs/api.rst,376] file system.  The environment will keep the compiled modules in memory like
[C,docs/api.rst,377] Python's `sys.modules`.  Unlike `sys.modules` however this cache is limited in
[C,docs/api.rst,378] size by default and templates are automatically reloaded.
[C,docs/api.rst,379] All loaders are subclasses of :class:`BaseLoader`.  If you want to create your
[C,docs/api.rst,380] own loader, subclass :class:`BaseLoader` and override `get_source`.
