[A,docs/api.rst,402] Bytecode Cache
[A,docs/api.rst,403] --------------
[A,docs/api.rst,404] 
[A,docs/api.rst,405] Jinja 2.1 and higher support external bytecode caching.  Bytecode caches make
[A,docs/api.rst,406] it possible to store the generated bytecode on the file system or a different
[A,docs/api.rst,407] location to avoid parsing the templates on first use.
[A,docs/api.rst,408] 
[A,docs/api.rst,409] This is especially useful if you have a web application that is initialized on
[A,docs/api.rst,410] the first request and Jinja compiles many templates at once which slows down
[A,docs/api.rst,411] the application.
[A,docs/api.rst,412] 
[A,docs/api.rst,413] To use a bytecode cache, instanciate it and pass it to the :class:`Environment`.
